Modifications made by the EdgeSlicer fork
-----------------------------------------

This is a trimmed copy, not the upstream file.  Upstream ColorSolver.cpp is
2024 lines; this copy keeps the candidate / kd-tree / Oklab core and drops the
rest.

Kept, essentially unchanged:

  * the sRGB <-> linear and sRGB <-> Oklab conversions
  * the chroma-dependent Oklab axis weights, the OklabSoftCap4Dark4 dark
    penalty, and ColorSolverMode / ColorSolverLookupMode
  * the candidate enumeration over a fixed unit budget
    (color_solver_total_units_for_component_count, color_solver_candidate_count,
    build_color_solver_candidates) and its string cache key
  * both kd-trees (linear sRGB and Oklab), their construction and their
    branch-and-bound queries, including the best/second-best bookkeeping that
    BlendClosestTwo needs
  * solve_color_solver_weights_for_target

Changed:

  * ColorSolverMixModel is deleted.  Upstream could mix through either
    pigment-painter (GPL-3.0, plus a 36 MiB generated lookup table) or
    prusa-fdm-mixer; neither library is vendored here.  mix_color_solver_
    components now calls the fork's own header-only mixer,
    src/libslic3r/filament_mixer_model.h (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Justin Hayes),
    chained pairwise in the same order and with the same weight accumulation as
    MixedFilamentManager::blend_color_multi, so the solver's prediction and the
    colour the user sees on the sidebar chip are the same number.
  * build_color_solver_candidates takes a ColorSolverConstraints (minimum and
    maximum share per used component, and a cap on how many components may be
    non-zero) so the enumeration can honour the batch dialog's existing
    per-component percentage limits directly, and a candidate budget that drops
    the unit lattice rather than enumerating an unbounded set.
  * solve_color_solver_candidate_for_target was added so a caller can read the
    winning mix's colour straight out of the candidate set.

Dropped entirely (not present in this copy):

  * the ordered-stack / contoning solver and ColorSolverCalibratedStackModel -
    the Beer-Lambert, TD-effective-alpha, adaptive-spectral and
    nearest-measured-sample stack models, the stack stretching and beam search,
    and mix_color_solver_ordered_stack
  * ColorSolverStackComponentRole
  * every reference to pigment-painter and prusa-fdm-mixer
